er  any of the three companions had with her  i wish any of the three of them would  confront her when she's pulling  bs because this is kind of what i meant  when i said it would have been okay if  the doctor was making mistakes that got  them all in danger and as long as  somebody is addressing that and the  characters aren't just letting it slide  and it never goes anywhere a scene like  this where asto says you are being  selfish you need to get a grip  is something that i needed now if people  really want to be super cool it'd be  like oh yeah man has to talk her down  there's no true vibe of that in this  scene somebody needed to call her out  for what she was trying to do it could  have been him it could have been anybody  it didn't have to be him it doesn't  matter but the fact that he did was a  good scene and the fact that that is  something that does not regularly happen  is what makes a lot of the stuff that  goes on with the doctor but the mistakes  she makes and the moral high horse she  has a tendency to get on become a  problem because the show never confronts  it it just does it and there's so many  great little moments like there's this  wonderful little moment between the two  of them where i'm the doctor  are you kidding sometimes  but not right now that's a great little  character response and it's the kind of  stuff i want from her more than we get  other than that as we get into the back  end look the the male pregnancy stuff  it's it's fine  it's cute it's fine it's a standard  birth oh i wasn't ready for this that  scene it's just with a guy it's like  fine whatever i do kind of appreciate  how it brings back the issue of with  ryan and his dad  and the his uh his hang ups around that  and how it evokes that they do deliver  that in another sort of hey  how do you feel about what's going on  scene which is a little bit clunky but  once yaz kind of opens the door for him  to talk about that i do i did feel that  ryan's uh explanation and his 